/target
# Cargo.lock IS committed. This workspace ships binaries (`pros`, `pros-gui`),
# and the other three Rust workspaces in the collection commit theirs too - the bare
# `Cargo.lock` line here was the library default `cargo new` writes, left in by mistake.

# Payload binaries are never tracked. The manifest says where to fetch them; a copy in
# the tree is a redistribution obligation and a stale mirror at the same time.
# See docs/DESIGN.md and the provenance check.
*.elf
*.bin
*.prx
*.sprx
*.pkg

# The Windows build directory, for the icon-bearing executable.
/target-win/

# Claude Code's per-person overrides. `settings.json` beside it IS shared - SELFish uses it to
# deny reads and edits of `escalation.*` - but the `.local` one is whoever is sitting here, and
# tracking it means their overrides arrive in everybody else's clone. SELFish had it committed
# as a byte-identical copy of the shared file, which is the shape this prevents.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Whatever the person editing this happens to run. None of it is anybody else's business,
# and every one of these has been committed to some repository by accident at least once.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
